Maybe the challenge expects me to realize that the ciphertext is provided in the challenge description or I'm missing something. Let me re-read the problem: 'We found a brand new type of encryption, can you break the secret code?' Perhaps the ciphertext is embedded in the challenge name or somewhere else. Or maybe I need to brute-force all possible single-character keys and see which one produces a valid picoCTF flag when decoded. But I still need the ciphertext!

Wait - maybe the file I'm looking at is a template, and the actual challenge has different values. Let me check if there's a way to get the actual ciphertext. Perhaps I should just try running the script as-is to see what happens.", "action": "shell", "cmd": "python3 ./challenge/new_caesar.py 2>&1"}
